//================================================================================
// HPVersusCamera.
//
// Camera SAFETY SHIM for multiplayer.
//
// WHY THIS EXISTS:
//   BaseCam is a PER-LEVEL SINGLETON (one per map), owned by its CamTarget and
//   bound to Level.PlayerHarryActor. harry.uc forces that shared camera onto
//   itself every tick (SetCameraMode(3) + InitTarget(self)). With two duelists
//   both doing that, the host camera is yanked between them every frame.
//
//   The fix is NOT to spawn a second BaseCam (its states re-couple to
//   PlayerHarry). The fix is to make sure ONLY the locally-rendered viewport
//   pawn ever touches the shared camera. Remote pawns (Player==None, or a
//   non-Viewport Player) must leave the camera alone.
//
// This is an Object (not an Actor): zero replication, zero spawn, no state
// machine. Just static helpers called from HPVersusHarry. Static functions run
// in the context of the caller, so they execute client-side when called from a
// client-owned pawn - no "simulated" modifier needed (and simulated on a
// non-Actor class can warn under strict compilers).
//
// See: hp2_ut_multiplayer_plan_ru_en.txt -> "4. ÐÐ°Ð¼ÐµÑÐ° / Phase 4".
//================================================================================

class HPVersusCamera based on Object
    abstract;

// True only for the locally-rendered player pawn. This is the same idiom used
// in PlayerPawn.uc and the existing HPVersusGame/HPVersusHarry code.
// NOTE: do NOT use bIsPlayer for this test - bots set bIsPlayer=True.
static function bool SafeToTouchCam(PlayerPawn P)
{
    return (P != None && P.Player != None && Viewport(P.Player) != None);
}

